## 3. The two breaches, measured before the repair (verbatim)

# qhslowifetch pass 5 -- the widened-mask breach (codex B1 = glm breach 1), MEASURED 2026-11-05 ~06:4xZ before its adjudication
mask7_table.run.sh -> mask7_table/ (scratch clone /tmp/gxqhs9 under a clone-local .MUTANT sentinel, restored, cmp-clean, rebuilt).
M7 = arm (b)'s test widened to `(cpu->pc & ~(uint64_t)7) != addr`.  Guest `mtlr r3; blr` (blr_witness.py, far breakpoint):
                    -T r3=0x02040003      -T r3=0x02040007      no -T (both)
  fix5 (base)       1 report, parks       1 report, parks       UNIMPLEMENTED, 1 line
  M7                1 report, parks       8278 reports          UNIMPLEMENTED, 1 line
The 79-row probe on M7: PPC_IFETCH_RESULT=79/79, CONTROL=OK, RED=none (mask7_table/probe79_M7.out).  So the breach is REAL: the
shipped composite cannot see a mask widened past bit 1, because T blr's 0x02040003 has bit 2 clear (pc & ~7 == addr == 0x02040000).
At 0x02040007 the prologue gives addr = 0x02040004, the fix compares 0x02040004 == addr and parks, M7 compares 0x02040000 != addr,
takes arm (b) and re-runs the slot.  Remedy both seats name: re-seed T blr at r3 = 0x02040007 (bits 0-2 set): the fix parks; ~1 gives
0x..06, ~2 gives 0x..05, ~7 gives 0x..00, the revert gives 0x..07 -- all != addr, all flood.

# qhslowifetch pass 5 -- Mythos breach 2 (MYTHOS.md, MYTHOS_r2.md), MEASURED 2026-11-05 ~08:3xZ before its repair
traodd_table.run.sh -> traodd_table/ (scratch clone /tmp/gxqhs10, clone-local .MUTANT, restored cmp-clean against GXEMUL-SEC, rebuilt,
cleared).  `T ra` (a -T continue from cpc700_pci's last word; no breakpoint, so read-ahead runs) entered at 0xfec00004 and at the
UNALIGNED 0xfec00005 (traodd_witness.py):
                          pc 0xfec00004                    pc 0xfec00005
  fix (repair 5)          pc 0xfec00008, 2 reports         pc 0xfec00009, 2 reports
  A1 `&& cpu->pc == addr` pc 0xfec00008, 2 reports         pc 0xfec00009, 1 report
  A2 `&& !(cpu->pc & 3)`  pc 0xfec00008, 2 reports         pc 0xfec00009, 1 report
  (every run exit 0; every halt names 0xfec00008; SRR0 and MSR unchanged; no checkstop or UNIMPLEMENTED text)
The 79-row probe on A1 and on A2: 79/79, CONTROL=OK, RED=none (traodd_table/probe79_A1.out, probe79_A2.out).  So the breach is REAL:
from an unaligned pc the read-ahead fetch reaches the failure block with pc != addr, the conjoined guard sends it on to arm (c), which
parks it at read-ahead time, and the real fetch's second report never comes.  Row: a `T ra odd` session (0xfec00005) pinning exit 0,
pc 0xfec00009 and two reports.

