measured before its adjudication (p3_20261105/table_p3, DHALT_NOTE.md; the ruling p3_20261105/ADJ_MYTHOS.md), placed the msr
rows and `T ra chkstop`; the other shapes are disclosed below.
  discloses, not claimed: arm (a)'s guard and its exit are claimed only at read-ahead depth 1, the only depth measured -- a
weakening of the guard, or a substitution of its exit (arm (b)'s refresh-and-return in place of the bare return), that differs
from the fix only at a deeper read-ahead is green on every row and is not claimed; MSR is rowed on every -T session, and a write
to a CPU field this block neither reads nor writes -- one that changes none of pc, SRR0, MSR or the reports -- is not claimed,
and neither is a write to running in arm (a) (R5_arun, MEASURED green in tables 5 and 6; the repair-pass-4 review): the real
fetch's second halt masks it on both read-ahead sessions, a window whose last word branches away would see it, and none is
