its low two bits cleared, because an unaligned pc keeps them through the translator's prologue (cpu->pc is assigned before addr
is aligned) -- from the debugger, and from guest code, since this fork's mtlr and its unconditional blr (X(bclr_20)) copy LR
without masking them (architecturally a branch ignores them: filed separately) -- and the bare compare sent such a pc into arm
(b), which re-ran the slot (`T blr` rows it now); arm (b) itself is reached only when the translation moved pc to an exception
vector, on no measured session; WITHOUT -T the guest-made unaligned fetch reads zeros and stops on the zero word, so no arm of
the block runs (MEASURED, p4_20261105/AC_NOTE.md) and no no-T `blr` session is rowed; arm (d) and the checkstop fallback (D6,
D9, D10): no fetch on pmppc reaches them -- MEASURED by a fetch at every 4-byte offset of every window `device list` names, MSR
0 and MSR[ME], each offset with evidence the word was fetched (det_20261104/window_sweep.out), and in the slack above RAM
(slack_sweep.out); their producer is a device declining an instruction fetch while running, which needs another machine (the
reconciliation's ROW 5, FILED pending X11); 64-bit CPUs; PPC603-class CPUs (their miss vector is 0x10); IR-on fetches whose
translation succeeds onto non-existent memory; a successful slow-path fetch with running already 0 (glm's `|| !running` widening
of the failure test) -- no measured single-CPU shape produces one: a -T data halt ends the run at the faulting load or store
(p3_20261105/DHALT_NOTE.md), and the one producer that measurement cannot see is another CPU mid-batch after memory.c's -T halt
cleared every CPU's running (#PPP).  THE READ-AHEAD CELL is measured on cpc700_pci (`T ra`, and with ME set `T ra me`); at the
other seven windows' last words the word a guest load records before the continue is 0x00000000, which decodes as unimplemented,
so no read-ahead past the window is issued (part 2: no halt report) -- MEASURED at that word, DERIVED for other values of those
registers: a window end inside a page puts the failing word in reach of read-ahead, and whether read-ahead happens depends on
the decoded word (cpc700_pci shows a valid non-branch word reaches it).  Read-ahead runs only on a free-running continue:
single-step disables it (measured, artifacts/qhslowifetch/p2r_20261105/extra_sessions.out), and so do instruction trace and any
set breakpoint (cpu_dyntrans.c's read-ahead condition, by code reading).  The RTC window ran twice and read 0 at +0xfc both
times.
  RE-ENTRY -- every exit returns before the slot's function pointer is replaced, so the slot stays untranslated.  Re-entry after
arm (a)'s exit is measured by `T ra`: the slot stays untranslated and the real fetch re-enters the arm in the same batch (the
second report).  Re-entry after arm (c)'s exit is untestable here: the park ends the batch and running is clear, so nothing
fetches the slot again; the `again` session therefore measures nothing about re-entry after a park and stands as the control
that the debugger survives step and continue on a halted CPU, its halt-count row the control that a -T halt is terminal for the
session.  W5's catch rides on the uninitialised instruction word: which rows red under W5 depends on the garbage decoded, though
some row must (a decoded word moves pc, traps, prints UNIMPLEMENTED or loops).  -T imprecision: a -T data halt earlier in the
same batch followed by a declined fetch takes arm (c), with no machine check (cosmetic; the debugger is entered either way). The
reconciliation's W7 (the read-ahead guard missing) is rowed by `T ra`; its W8 (the running-1 arm missing) and W9 (a wrong
machine check) have no row on pmppc: they need its ROW 5 (FILED pending X11).  On this 82-row probe the pre-fix build scores 40
