For example, ~0x40003 preserves bits 2 and 3 but clears bit 18. T blr then compares 0x02000004 against 0x02040004 and exposes the edit. The particular ~0x13 example is valid; restrict the explanation to higher bits absent from the measured addresses. The disclosed class itself is not counted as a new breach.

